  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Envelope 2 - Strengthening the resilience of affected communities in Afrin and Azaz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is designed to strengthen the self-reliance and resilience of the affected communities by improving their access to livelihood opportunities and basic services through the integration of ERL, FSL and Protection related activities. The intervention targets Jandairis and A&#x2019;zaz cities along with four camps, all locations classified as underserved according to the current OCHA allocation with identified needs aligned with Envelop 2 of 2022 SA-1. The project consists of 3 pillars: (1) delivery of vocational trainings (2) provision of livelihood opportunities in the form of small-business grants and apprenticeships and (3) provision of protection services to reduce the affected communities&#x2019; protection risks through the establishment of solidarity groups and delivery of case management. Due to the earthquake, activities related to ERL and FSL were not able to continue (vocational training and mentorship). SBG (both ERL and FSL) are continuing along with Protection. A new output under FSL was added for MPCA.</narrative>
  </description>
